---
layout: page.njk
title: Home
description: The personal site of Niall Bell, a nature photographer, writer, and environmentalist from England, living in BC.
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/static/css/swiper-bundle.min.css' | url }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/static/css/leaflet.css' | url }}"/>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/static/css/MarkerCluster.css' | url }}"/>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/static/css/MarkerCluster.Default.css' | url }}"/>

<div class="home-hero-wrapper">
  {% if collections.homeGallery and collections.homeGallery.length %}
  {% set slides = collections.homeGallery[0].content | extractImages %}
  {% if slides.length %}
  <div class="home-slideshow-fs">
    <div class="swiper home-swiper">
      <div class="swiper-wrapper">
        {% for img in slides %}
        <div class="swiper-slide">
          <img src="{{ img.src }}" alt="{{ img.alt }}" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="swiper-button-prev"></div>
      <div class="swiper-button-next"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}

  <section class="home-hero-overlay">
    <h1 class="home-title">Niall Bell</h1>
    <p class="home-intro">
      I'm Niall, a nature photographer and environmentalist from the UK, based in British Columbia, Canada. I spend my time documenting the wildlife and wild places of my surroundings and sharing the beauty of the natural world through photography and writing.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-hint">
      <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M7 13l5 5 5-5M7 6l5 5 5-5"/></svg>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<div class="home-stats-row">
  <div class="home-block-header">
    <p class="section-label">Welcome</p>
  </div>
    <div class="home-stats-card">
    <div class="home-stats-content">
      <div class="home-stats-message">
	      <p class="home-stats-text">niallbell.com is the digital home of my photography, videography, and writing. I built and maintain the website myself in my spare time with the hope of sharing inspiring photographs and interesting writing.</p>
        <p class="home-stats-text">In an era of social media and AI, human visitors to independent websites are becoming increasingly rare, so thank you for being here.</p>

        <details class="welcome-expansion">
          <summary>Learn more about how your visit matters <span class="expansion-arrow">→</span></summary>
          <div class="expansion-wrapper">
            <div class="expansion-content">
              <p class="home-stats-text">I worry that as AI crawlers scrape the web and funnel content into chatbots, the motivation to maintain sites like this will slowly fade away. I've built measures into this site to block those crawlers, because the work I put in here was never meant to train a model. I don't rely on ad revenue, and I don't even serve ads, but many websites do. Without real human visitors, those sites don't get paid, and when they don't get paid, they're forced to find other ways to make money, which puts strain authentic writing. If these values resonate with you, consider browsing the web a little more directly, and let the surfing be yours. Thank you.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
      
      <div class="home-stats-right-col">
        <div class="home-stats-heart" data-tooltip="This total reflects visits to every page across the site. Each visitor is counted only once per session, though returns on subsequent days will count again. Search engine crawlers are also permitted and may occasionally contribute to the total.">
          <canvas id="heart-canvas" width="400" height="400" style="position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); pointer-events: none; z-index: 1;"></canvas>
          <div class="heart-counter-content" style="position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); z-index: 3; text-align: center; pointer-events: none;">
            <span id="visitor-count" class="heart-counter-value" style="display: block; font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 800; color: #fff; line-height: 1; height: 50%">...</span>
            <span class="heart-counter-label" style="display: block; font-size: 0.6rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); margin-top: 2px;">HUMAN <br> VISITS</span>
          </div>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="120" height="120" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" style="position: relative; z-index: 2;"><path d="M12 21.35l-1.45-1.32C5.4 15.36 2 12.28 2 8.5 2 5.42 4.42 3 7.5 3c1.74 0 3.41.81 4.5 2.09C13.09 3.81 14.76 3 16.5 3 19.58 3 22 5.42 22 8.5c0 3.78-3.4 6.86-8.55 11.54L12 21.35z"/></svg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% if collections.featuredGalleries and collections.featuredGalleries.length %}
<div class="home-posts">
  <div class="home-block-header">
    <p class="section-label">Featured Galleries</p>
    <a href="{{ '/photography/' | url }}" class="view-all">All photography →</a>
  </div>
  <div class="story-list">
    {% for gallery in collections.featuredGalleries | limit(3) %}
    <a href="{{ gallery.url | url }}" class="story-card">
      <div class="story-card-img">
        {% if gallery.data.coverImage %}
        <img src="{{ gallery.data.coverImage }}" alt="{{ gallery.data.title }}" loading="lazy">
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="story-card-body">
        <div class="post-card-meta">
          {% if gallery.date %}<time class="post-card-date" datetime="{{ gallery.date | isoDate }}">{{ gallery.date | readableDate }}</time>{% endif %}
          {% if gallery.data.tags %}
          <div class="post-card-tags">
            {% for tag in gallery.data.tags | limit(2) %}<span class="tag">{{ tag }}</span>{% endfor %}
          </div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        <div class="story-card-title">{{ gallery.data.title }}</div>
        {% if gallery.data.excerpt %}
        <div class="story-card-desc">{{ gallery.data.excerpt }}</div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}

{% if collections.posts and collections.posts.length %}
<div class="home-posts">
  <div class="home-block-header">
    <p class="section-label">Recent writing</p>
    <a href="{{ '/blog/' | url }}" class="view-all">All writing →</a>
  </div>
  <div class="story-list">
    {% for post in collections.posts | limit(3) %}
    <a href="{{ post.url | url }}" class="story-card">
      <div class="story-card-img">
        {% if post.data.coverImage %}
        <img src="{{ post.data.coverImage }}" alt="{{ post.data.title }}" loading="lazy">
        {% else %}
        <div class="post-card-placeholder" style="width: 100%; height: 100%; background: var(--color-surface);"></div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="story-card-body">
        <div class="post-card-author">Niall Bell</div>
        <div class="post-card-meta">
          {% if post.date %}<time class="post-card-date" datetime="{{ post.date | isoDate }}">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</time>{% endif %}
          {% if post.data.tags %}
          <div class="post-card-tags">
            {% for tag in post.data.tags | limit(2) %}<span class="tag">{{ tag }}</span>{% endfor %}
          </div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        <div class="story-card-title">{{ post.data.title }}</div>
        {% if post.data.excerpt %}<div class="story-card-desc">{{ post.data.excerpt }}</div>{% endif %}
      </div>
    </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}

